    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen in a changed file, calling `MiniDiff.toggle()` twice, will set mini.diff in a state where it is enabled, but wont show any signs in the gutter until the window is resized, a changed line is focused, or other rerenders.\n\n### Reproduction\n\nUse newest mini.nvim, open any changed file. Initially mini.diff will mark changed lines. Executing `lua MiniDiff.toggle()` twice, will have the diff enabled but hidden, until another rerender.",
